---
description: BPMN interoperability, signed service packages, migration, semantic registry, assisted service, risk and privacy extensions
alwaysApply: false
---
- Temporal remains the durable workflow runtime; BPMN is import/export over the canonical ServiceForm Workflow Model.
- Never silently migrate active cases to new workflow/config versions.
- Promote service configuration through signed `.sfpackage` artifacts; never embed secrets.
- Assisted channels must keep `applied_by` distinct from `applied_for`.
- Reuse CMP-058 canonical semantic elements for common government fields.
- Risk/AI integrity signals cannot independently reject or penalize a citizen.
- Privacy Centre orchestrates owner-domain tasks; it must not directly mutate foreign tables.
- Read `specs/world-class-extensions.yaml` before implementing CMP-056..CMP-061 or related cross-cutting capabilities.
